# Row B7: capability representation (x/apibench/b7). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./x/apibench/b7
BENCH=BenchmarkAPI/Capabilities
REF=array
AUTO_KEY=b7
# the benchmark configuration: this row is one of the MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE API shapes.
# Only one shape can be the API, so a shape the API did not take is a loser
# in §9.4(5)'s sense and cannot be retained as a profile the way a §9.1 arm
# can.
CLASS=B
#
# `git worktree add <path> d802b9e4e8c9` restores every shape this row
# measured, which is what makes a re-ratification on a pinned host still
# possible.
REMOVED=retired
ADR=7
TITLE="Capability representation: array of support records or packed bitmask, with both Require forms (B7)"
# Both representations hold the whole 39-feature inventory and answer the same
# requirement with the same verdict, so BenchmarkAPI/Capabilities compares the
# storage alone. The other half of §9.2's evidence for the row is the
# expressiveness matrix, and it is not a number of nanoseconds: the packed
# representation is 32 bytes against the array's 1024 (TestFootprint) and
# cannot hold the message contract's Support.Note at all, so a failed
# requirement against a conditionally supported feature cannot name the
# condition §4.8 requires the driver to state. That is the misuse table's
# conditionnotnamed column, and it is the row's finding.
#
# Both RequireAtLeast and RequireAny ship (§4.8), and Rank is deliberately not
# the levels' declaration order: volatile emulation ranks below conditional
# support and is excluded from durability requirements outright — an exclusion
# that is redundant under the current ranks and pinned as such
# (adr/ADR-017-assumptions.md).
#
# What the row does NOT prototype: §4.8's Limits half — Limit[T]{Value, Known}
# and the Limits struct, whose rule is that an unknown limit is never an
# overloaded zero. The row is the per-feature Support table (level, scope,
# note) only. Limits are representation-independent, so their absence does not
# skew the array-against-bitmask comparison, but A24 must not read the row as
# having exercised that contract; whoever binds it needs its own cases.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="struct with array-backed 'Has'; both Require forms (Has() ns; expressiveness matrix)"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: x/apibench/b7 has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch, and its four rows per kind are the lookup and the three Require
# forms.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="Has RequireAtLeast RequireAny RequireBoth"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op"
# The row does not turn on ns/op: the two representations differ in what they
# can EXPRESS -- a 32-byte packed field cannot hold §4.8's note, a 1024-byte
# array can -- and §4.8's Limits/Limit[T] half is not prototyped here at all,
# so the row must not be read as covering it (hack/FOLLOWUPS.md).
CRITERION_GAP="expressiveness=x/apibench/scoring scorecard.json, which carries what each representation can express (§4.8's Limits half is prototyped in no family at all)"
